# Godot 캐시
.godot/

# 엔진 바이너리 (170MB — 커밋 금지)
Godot_v*.exe

# 임시
*.tmp

# 내보낸 빌드 — 웹 하나가 39MB. 산출물이라 리포에 안 남긴다.
# 프리셋(export_presets.cfg)은 커밋한다 — 그게 있어야 아무 데서나 같은 빌드가 나온다.
build/

# 도구가 쓰는 락 파일 — 로컬 상태라 리포에 안 남긴다.
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock

# git worktree — 자기 브랜치에 이미 커밋돼 있다. 여기 넣으면 같은 파일이 두 번 들어간다.
.claude/worktrees/

# MCP 설정 — 엔진·Aseprite 실행 경로가 이 PC 절대경로로 박혀 있다.
.mcp.json

# Scratch screenshots dropped at the repo root — reference shots pasted in during a round, never assets.
# **A png and its `.import` sidecar are ONE thing and both halves must be ignored together.** Godot writes
# the sidecar next to the image on import; ignoring only the png leaves the sidecar tracked, and then the
# repo carries a file whose `source_file=` points at an image that is not in the repo — the same mistake
# already made once under `tools/blender/`, recorded further down.
# ⚠ **Both entries are root-anchored (`/`)** so they cannot swallow an `image.png` that a future asset
#  folder legitimately tracks. `image copy.png` was left unanchored and half-covered until 2026-08-27.
# ⚠⚠ **An ignore rule does not untrack what is already tracked.** `image copy.png.import` was committed
#  before this rule existed and is still in the index; it needs a `git rm --cached` to actually leave.
# Note: `export_presets.cfg` also names `image.png, image copy.png` in its exclude_filter, so an exported
#  build drops them even if a working copy has them on disk. That filter is the build's half of the same
#  decision — if a name here changes, change it there too.
/image.png
/image.png.import
/image copy.png
/image copy.png.import

# 에셋 생성 후보 — 한 번에 수십 장씩 나온다. 🔴 **고른 것만** assets/ 로 옮겨 커밋한다.
tools/pixel/out/

# 파이썬 도구 캐시
tools/pixel/__pycache__/

# 🔴 검증자가 잠깐 만드는 계측기. `_` 로 시작하면 러너의 그물 스캔에도 안 걸린다.
#  ⚠ **검증자가 끝나고 지우는 것이 계약이지만, 그 전에 누가 커밋하면 딸려 들어간다** —
#   실제로 2026-08-07에 verify-run 이 도는 중에 세 개가 커밋됐다. 규율이 아니라 여기서 막는다.
tests/_*.gd
tests/_*.gd.uid

# 촬영 원본 — 45MB. 유튜브에 올라가는 산출물이라 리포에 안 남긴다.
*.mp4

# net round logs — the round result already lives in the commit message.
.rounds/

# The instruments' own output. **The SCRIPTS are tracked and the frames are not** — a shooter rewrites its
# whole frame set on every run, sixty-odd files a round, and a screenshot that is regenerated by one
# command is not a thing to keep a history of.
# ⚠ `shoot_loop` itself is deleted; its frames are still sitting in that folder, so the rule stays until
#  they do not.
tools/shot/fx_*.png
tools/shot/fx_*.png.import
tools/shot/loop_*.png
tools/shot/loop_*.png.import

# Blender's own renders. `island_build.py`, `turntable.py` and `grab_viewport.py` each write to a
# hardcoded path in that folder and overwrite it on every run, so a frame deleted without this rule is
# back on the next run.
# **The `.import` sidecars too** — ignoring only the png once left the sidecars tracked, and they were
#  committed twice before anyone noticed. The engine regenerates them on the next import.
tools/blender/*.png
tools/blender/*.png.import
